-- title:
--   Wronskians of a spanning family as a base-point-free subsystem of |2D+K|
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and write $\bar F_N$ for [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldBar N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L111), the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of level $N$; assume the predicate `HasCanonicalDivisor` for $\bar F_N/\overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e. that every nonzero $\omega\in\Omega[\bar F_N/\overline{\mathbb Q}]$ admits a divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\,\omega$. Let $r\in\mathbb N$ and let $s\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,r\to\bar F_N$ have all entries nonzero; let $D$ be a divisor (a finitely supported $\mathbb Z$-valued function on places) with $2g+1\le\deg D$, where $g$ is `genusFF`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-dimension of $H^1(0)$, and assume the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-span of the range of $s$ equals $L(D)=\{f:\ v(f)\le\exp(D v)\ \text{for all places } v\}$, the Riemann–Roch space of $D$. Let $x\in\bar F_N$ satisfy $dx\ne 0$, and let $K_x=$ `canonicalDivisorOf` $hx$ be the chosen canonical divisor attached to $dx$. Put $W_{ij}=\mathrm{diffCoeff}_x\bigl(s_i\,ds_j-s_j\,ds_i\bigr)$, the element $g$ chosen with $s_i\,ds_j-s_j\,ds_i=g\,dx$ (and $0$ if none exists). The conclusion is twofold: every $W_{ij}$ lies in $L(2D+K_x)$; and for every place $w$ there are indices $i,j$ with $W_{ij}\ne 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_w(W_{ij})+(2D+K_x)(w)=0$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the classical statement that for $\deg D\ge 2g+1$ the Wronskians of a spanning family of $L(D)$ — the Plücker coordinates of the Gauss map of the embedding $\varphi_D$ — are sections of $2D+K$ cutting out no base point, the second clause recording that at each place some Wronskian attains the exact order $-(2D+K_x)(w)$. It is used in the height comparison [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_abs_absLogHeight_regVal_sub_pointHt_add_pointHt_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_abs_absLogHeight_regVal_sub_pointHt_add_pointHt_le) for the degree-zero divisor class group of $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZero_diffCoeff_wronskian_mem_riemannRochSpace_and_exists_ord_add_eq_zero.lean

